                  %a{:href => "#of_an_object_in_a_symmetric_monoidal_category"} Of an object in a symmetric monoidal category
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#HomotopyCardinality"}
                    Homotopy cardinality (
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mn ∞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                    \-groupoid cardinality)
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#of_posets_groupoids_and_categories"} Of posets, groupoids and categories
                %ul
                  %li
                    %a{:href => "#LECharOfCategory"} Of finite categories
                  %li
                    %a{:href => "#LECharOfEnrichedCat"} Of enriched and higher categories
              %li
                %a{:href => "#properties"} Properties
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#UnderHomotopyColimits"} Compatibility with homotopy colimits
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#RelationBetweenDefinitions"} Relations between the various definitions
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#relation_between_euler_characteristic_and_groupoid_cardinality"}
                    Relation between Euler characteristic and
                    = succeed "-groupoid" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mn ∞
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#basic_relations_for_euler_characteristics_of_topological_spaces"} Basic relations for Euler characteristics of topological spaces
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#gaussbonnet_theorem"} Gauss-Bonnet theorem
              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_concepts"} Related concepts
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %strong Euler characteristic
            of an object is – if it exists – its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} categorical
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %h3#of_a_chain_complex Of a chain complex
          %p
            There are two definitions of the Euler characteristic of a chain complex. Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+ring"} commutative ring
            and let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
            of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modules"} modules
          #EulerCharOfChainComplexPointset.num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              If each
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_n
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finitely+generated+object"} finitely generated
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+object"} projective
              %strong Euler characteristic
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              is the alternating sum of their
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ranks"} ranks
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi χ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi n
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi rk
                      %mi R
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi n
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\chi(V)
                    \\,\coloneqq\,
                    \\sum_{n \in \mathbb{Z}} (-1)^n \, rk_R V_n
                    \\,.
          #EulerCharOfChainComplex.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              If the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homology+group"} homology
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              consists of finitely generated projective modules, then the
              %strong Euler characteristic
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              is the alternating sum of its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Betti+number"} Betti numbers
              (the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ranks"} ranks
              of its homology modules), if this is finite:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi χ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi n
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi rk
                      %mi R
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\chi(V)
                    \\,\coloneqq\,
                    \\sum_{n \in \mathbb{Z}} (-1)^n \, rk_R H_n(V)
                    \\,.
          %p
            When both of these are defined, they are equal. This is a consequence of the functoriality of the categorical definition (Definition
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EulerCharInSymMonCat"}
          #InvariantUnderQIso.num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              Definition
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EulerCharOfChainComplex"}
              shows that the Euler characteristic of chain complexes is invariant under the natural notion of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} equivalence
              of chain complexes: (zig-zags of)
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-isomorphism"} quasi-isomorphisms
          %h3#OfATopologicalSpace
            Of a topological space (or
            = succeed "-groupoid)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          #EulerCharOfTopSpace.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              some
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              is the Euler characteristic, according to Def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EulerCharOfChainComplex"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homology"} homology
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
              (for instance
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+homology"} singular homology
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Betti+numbers"} Betti numbers
            #eq:FormulaForTopologicalSpaceAsAltSumOfBettiNumbers.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi χ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mo ≔
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %munder
                              %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                              %mrow
                                %mi n
                                %mo ∈
                                %mi ℕ
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mi n
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %msub
                              %mi rk
                              %mi ℤ
                            %msub
                              %mi H
                              %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mo =
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %munder
                              %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                              %mrow
                                %mi n
                                %mo ∈
                                %mi ℕ
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mi n
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %msub
                              %mi dim
                              %mi ℚ
                            %msub
                              %mi H
                              %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mi ℚ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    \\chi(X)
                    \&amp;
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    \\sum_{n \in \mathbb{N}}
                    \\,
                    (-1)^n
                    \\,
                    rk_{\mathbb{Z}} H_n(X, \mathbb{Z})
                    \\\
                    \&amp;
                    \\;=\;
                    \\sum_{n \in \mathbb{N}}
                    \\,
                    (-1)^n
                    \\,
                    dim_{\mathbb{Q}} H_n(X, \mathbb{Q})
                    \\end{aligned}
                    \\,.
          %p
            This is shown for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo =
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R = \mathbb{Z}
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integral+cohomology"}> integral cohomology
            ), and equivalently for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo =
                  %mi ℚ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R = \mathbb{Q}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+numbers"} rational numbers
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+cohomology"}> rational cohomology
            ).
            %br>/
            (Choosing a ring with torsion, however, might result in a different “Euler characteristic”.)
          %p
            This definition is usually known as the
            = succeed "." do
              %strong Euler-Poincaré formula
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              This is the special case of the formula for the
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lefschetz+number"} Lefschetz number
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:FormulaForTopologicalSpaceAsAltSumOfBettiNumbers"} (1)
              is the Lefschetz number of the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+map"} identity map
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "Lefschetz+trace+formula#LefschetzNumber"} there
          %p Historically earlier was:
          #EulerCharOfCWComplex.num_defn
            %h6#definitionproposition Definition/Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              be a finite
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-complex"} CW-complex
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi cell
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cell(X)_k
              for the set of its
              = succeed "-cells." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi χ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi cell
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\chi(X)
                    \\;=\;
                    \\sum_{k \in \mathbb{N}} (-1)^k \vert cell(X)_k \vert
                    \\,.
          %p
            This is equivalently the Euler characteristic of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cellular+homology"} cellular
            chain complex of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            according to Definition
            = succeed "." do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EulerCharOfChainComplexPointset"}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            can be computed with cellular homology, this Euler characteristic agrees with the previous one.
          %p
            In the special case that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surface"} surface
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EulerCharOfCWComplex"}
            reduces to the historical definition by
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Leonhard+Euler"} Leonhard Euler
          #EulerCharOfSurface.num_defn
            %h6#definitionproposition_2 Definition/Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              be a convex
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polyhedron"} polyhedron
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi χ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi Vertices
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi Edges
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi Faces
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\chi(X)
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    \\vert Vertices(X)\vert
                    \-
                    \\vert Edges(X)\vert
                    +
                    \\vert Faces(X)\vert
                    \\;\in\;
                    \\mathbb{Z}
                    \\,,
            %p
              hence the number of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertices"} vertices
              minus the number of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/edges"} edges
              plus the number of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/faces"} faces
              in the polyhedron.
          %p
            In particular if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            may be embedded into the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-sphere"} 2-sphere
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 2
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi Vertices
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi Edges
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi Faces
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  2 = \vert Vertices(X)\vert - \vert Edges(X)\vert +
                  \\vert Faces(X)\vert
                  \\,.
          %p
            By removing one point from the 2-sphere not contained in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/planar+graph"} planar graph
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/face"} face
            less than
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            had (the one containing the point which was removed). Hence
          #EulerFormulaForPlanarGraphs.num_cor
            %h6#corollary Corollary
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euler+formula+for+planar+graphs"}> Euler formula for planar graphs
                )
            %p
              For a planar
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graph"} graph
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
              we have
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi Vertices
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
