          %h3#of_an_object_in_a_symmetric_monoidal_category Of an object in a symmetric monoidal category
          %p All the definitions considered so far can be subsumed by the following general abstract one.
          #EulerCharInSymMonCat.num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              The Euler characteristic of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dualizable+object"} dualizable object
              in a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
              is its categorical
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trace"} trace
              of its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity"} identity
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
          %p
            Explicitly, this means the Euler characteristic of an object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is the composite
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi η
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mo *
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo ≅
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mo *
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi X
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi ε
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \xrightarrow{\eta} X \otimes X^* \xrightarrow{\cong} X^* \otimes X \xrightarrow{\varepsilon} S
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi η
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ε
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varepsilon
            are the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+of+an+adjunction"} unit
            and counit of the dual pair
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,X^*)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is the unit object of the symmetric monoidal category. This subsumes the previous definitions as follows:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                In the category of chain complexes over a ring
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi X
                          %mo *
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi n
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi Hom
                          %mi R
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mi n
                        %mo ,
                        %mi R
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X^*)_n = Hom_R(X_{-n},R)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi η
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta
                picks out
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                        %mi x
                        %mo ⊗
                        %msup
                          %mi x
                          %mo *
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sum x \otimes x^*
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{x\}
                encompasses a basis for each
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_n
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{x^*\}
                is the dual basis.
              %p
                The symmetry isomorphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi Y
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mo ≅
                      %mi Y
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \otimes Y \xrightarrow{\cong} Y \otimes X
                introduces a sign
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi y
                        %mo ↦
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mi y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi y
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi x
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\otimes y \mapsto (-1)^{|y|} y\otimes x
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
                for each
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
                of even degree and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} -1
                for each
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
                of odd degree. Thus we recover Def.
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EulerCharOfChainComplexPointset"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                itself in degree zero, so that we see
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi χ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi(X)
                only as an element of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                (so, for instance, the Euler characteristic in this sense of a rank-
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                free
                = succeed "-module" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi ℤ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi p
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbb{Z}/p)
            %li
              %p
                In the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+category"} derived category
                of chain complexes over
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EulerCharOfChainComplex"}
          %p
            The Euler characteristic of a topological space or
            = succeed "-groupoid" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %em directly
            with this approach, without a detour into homology. Namely, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is any
            = succeed "," do
              %span.newWikiWord
                Euclidean Neighborhood Retract
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Euclidean+Neighborhood+Retract"} ?
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW+complex"} CW complex
            or a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/suspension+spectrum"} suspension spectrum
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo +
                    %mn ∞
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma_+^\infty X
            is dualizable in the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+category"} stable homotopy category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+spectrum"} Thom spectrum
            of its stable
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normal+bundle"} normal bundle
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+collapse+map"} Thom collapse map
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi π
                      %mn 0
                      %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0^s(S) = \mathbb{Z}
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#DoldPuppe"} DoldPuppe, corollary 4.6
          %p
            Since the categorical definition is purely in terms of the symmetric monoidal structure, Euler characteristics are preserved by any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+functor"} symmetric monoidal functor
            (as long as enough of its structure maps are isomorphisms). Since chains and homology can be made into symmetric monoidal functors, it follows that all the ways of defining the Euler characteristic of a space agree.
          %p
            See (
            %a{:href => "#PontoShulman"}> PontoShulman
            ) and the discussion at
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+spectrum"} Thom spectrum
            for more on this.
          %h3#HomotopyCardinality
            Homotopy cardinality (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            \-groupoid cardinality)
          %p
            The
            %a{:href => "OfATopologicalSpace"} above
            Euler characteristic of a topological space is the alternating
            %em sum
            over sizes of
            %em homology
            groups. Similar in construction is the alternating
            %em product
            of sizes of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+group"} homotopy groups
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid+cardinality"} ∞-groupoid cardinality
            or
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+cardinality"} homotopy cardinality
            \. But
            %a{:href => "RelationBetweenDefinitions"} below
            we shall see that Euler characteristic of higher categories interpolates between this homotopical and the above homological notion.
          #EulerCharOfSpaceHomotopically.num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              \/
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy type
              \/
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ∞-groupoid
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+cardinality"} homotopy cardinality
              or
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid+cardinality"} ∞-groupoid cardinality
              is – if it exists – the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+number"} rational number
              given by the alternating product of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cardinality"} cardinalities
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+group"} homotopy groups
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi χ
                      %mi homotop
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi π
                          %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %munderover
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi k
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\chi_{homotop}(X)
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    \\sum_{[x] \in \pi_0(X)}
                    \\prod_{k =1}^\infty (|\pi_k(X,x)|)^{(-1)^k}
                    \\,.
          %h3#of_posets_groupoids_and_categories Of posets, groupoids and categories
          %p
            The process of sending a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            to its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization+of+categories"} geometric realization of categories
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo ∈
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\vert C \vert} \in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
