              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ≃
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \simeq
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ∞Grpd
            is a way to
            %em present
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological spaces
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ∞-groupoids
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vert C \vert
            as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+fibrant+replacement"} Kan fibrant replacement
            of
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal solution
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+inverse"} weakly inverting
            all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphisms
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p
            Up to the relevant notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} equivalence in an (infinity,1)-category
            (which is
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalence"} weak homotopy equivalence
            %em every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ∞-groupoid
            arises as the
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization+of+categories"} geometric realization
            of a category. In fact one can assume the category to be a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomason+model+structure"} Thomason model structure
          %p
            Since the combinatorial data in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            and all the more in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is much smaller than in that of its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+fibrant+replacement"} Kan fibrant replacement
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vert C \vert
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi χ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi(\vert C \vert)
            already from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            itself. This is indeed the case:
          %h4#LECharOfCategory Of finite categories
          #EulerCharOfCat.num_defn
            %h6#definition_6 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              be a finite
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              %strong weighting
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi k
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi ob
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℚ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    k^{(-)} \colon ob C \to \mathbb{Q}
            %p satsifying
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∀
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ob
                    %mi C
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi b
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ob
                        %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %msup
                      %mi k
                      %mi b
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\forall a \in ob C \;:\; \sum_{b \in ob C} \vert C(a,b) \vert k^b
                    \= 1
                    \\,,
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vert C(a,b)\vert
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cardinality"} cardinality
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-set"} hom-set
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(a,b)
              %strong coweighting
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is a weighting on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite category
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mi op
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^{op}
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              admits both a weighting
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msup
                      %mi k
                      %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{k^a\}
              and a coweighting
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi k
                        %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{k_a\}
              %strong Euler characteristic
              is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi χ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ob
                        %mi C
                    %msup
                      %mi k
                      %mi a
                    %mo =
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ob
                        %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mi k
                      %mi a
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℚ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\chi(C) := \sum_{a \in ob C} k^a = \sum_{a \in ob C} k_a
                    \\;\;\;
                    \\in \mathbb{Q}
                    \\,.
          %p
            The definition of Euler characteristic of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} posets
            appears for instance in (
            %a{:href => "#Rota"}> Rota
            ). For
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoids
            it has been amplified in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#BaezDolan"} BaezDolan
            = succeed ")," do
              %a{:href => "#Leinster"} Leinster
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              Notice that this
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi χ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi(C)
              is in general not an
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integer"} integer
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+number"} rational number
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "RelationBetweenDefinitions"} below
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi χ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi(C)
              coincides with the topological Euler characteristic
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi χ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi(\vert C \vert)
              of its
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization+of+categories"} geometric realization
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi χ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi(C)
              is.
          %h4#LECharOfEnrichedCat Of enriched and higher categories
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            be an good enrichment category (for instance a
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosmos"} cosmos
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo :
                  %mi V
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  |-| : V \to \mathbb{R}
                  \\,.
          %p
            Then the above formula for the Euler characteristic of a category verbatim generalizes to
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+categories"} enriched categories
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo =
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V =
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FinSet"} FinSet
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo :
                  %mi FinSet
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} |-| : FinSet \to \mathbb{R}
            the ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cardinality"} cardinality
            operation.
          %p
            Since
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+infinity-categories"} strict infinity-categories
            can be understood as arising from iterative enrichment
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Str
                  %mn 2
                  %mi Cat
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi Cat
                  %mo −
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Str2Cat \simeq Cat-Cat
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Str
                  %mn 3
                  %mi Cat
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi Str
                  %mn 2
                  %mi Cat
                  %mo −
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Str3Cat \simeq Str2Cat-Cat
          %p
            etc, this gives a notion of Euler characteristic of strict
            = succeed "-categories," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+infinity-groupoid"} strict infinity-groupoids
          %p
            One should be able to show that applied to strict
            = succeed "-groupoids" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+cardinality"} homotopy cardinality
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#UnderHomotopyColimits Compatibility with homotopy colimits
          %p
            Euler characteristic behaves well with respect to the basic operations in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              In a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triangulated+category"} triangulated category
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dualizable+object"} dualizable objects
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Y
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Z
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X, Y, Z
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Z
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    Z &amp;\to&amp; Y
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    X &amp;\to&amp; W
                    }
            %p
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pushout"} homotopy pushout
              %a{:href => "EulerCharInSymMonCat"} tractial Euler characteristic
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              exists and is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi χ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi χ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                    %mi χ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo −
                    %mi χ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\chi(W) = \chi(X) + \chi(Y) - \chi(Z)
                    \\,.
          %p
            This is due to (
            %a{:href => "#May"}> May, 1991
            ).
          %h3#RelationBetweenDefinitions Relations between the various definitions
          %p The following propositions assert that and how the various definitions of Euler characteristics all suitably agree when thez jointly apply.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+space"} compact
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
              let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi P
                      %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P_T(X)
              be the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
              of inclusions of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplices"} simplices
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triangulation"} triangulation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi P
                      %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P_T(X)
              coincides with the Euler characteristic of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              as a topological space
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi χ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi χ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi P
                      %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\chi(X) = \chi(P_T(X))
                    \\,.
          %p
            This appears as (
            %a{:href => "#Stanley"}> Stanley, 3.8
            ).
          %p
            The following proposition asserts that the definition
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EulerCharOfCat"}
            of Euler characteristic of a category is indeed consistent, in that it does compute the Euler characteristic, def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EulerCharOfTopSpace"}
            of the corresponding
            = succeed "-groupoid:" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          #PosteEulerCharGiveSpaceCharUnderRealization.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              be a finite
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
              or, slightly more generally, a finite
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/skeleton"} skeletal
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              with no nontrivial
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endomorphism"} endomorphisms
            %p
              Write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo ∈
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vert C \vert \in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ≃
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \simeq
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ∞Grpd
              for its
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization+of+categories"} geometric realization
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi χ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi χ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\chi(C) = \chi(\vert C \vert)
                    \\,.
          %p
            For posets this is due to Philipp Hall, appearing as ([Stanley, prop. 3.8.5]). For finite categories this is (
            %a{:href => "#Leinster"}> Leinster, cor. 1.5, prop. 2.11
            ).
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/suspension+spectrum"} suspension spectrum
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Σ
                      %mn ∞
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Spec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Sigma^\infty X \in Ho(Spec)
            %p
              as an object in the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+category"} stable homotopy category
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EulerCharInSymMonCat"}
              coincides with its topological Euler characteristic, def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EulerCharOfTopSpace"}
          %p This is due to … (?)
          .query
            %p
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Shulman"}> Mike
              \: Can the Euler characteristic of a category be recovered as the trace for a dualizable object in some symmetric monoidal category?
          %h3#relation_between_euler_characteristic_and_groupoid_cardinality
            Relation between Euler characteristic and
            = succeed "-groupoid" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %p
            For topological space /
            = succeed "-groupoids," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %a{:href => "#OfATopologicalSpace"} homological Euler characteristic
            as well as the notion of
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#HomotopyCardinality"} homotopy cardinality
          %p
            The latter looks a bit like the “exponential” of the former, so while similar to some extent they are very different notions, taken on face value. Still, the
            %a{:href => "LECharOfCategory"} Euler characteristic of a category
            or rather that
            %a{:href => "LECharOfEnrichedCat"} of a higher category
            does interpolate between the two notions:
          #ReproducingGroupoidCardinality.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_5 Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              a finite
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EulerCharOfCat"}
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EulerCharOfSpaceHomotopically"}
              or
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid+cardinality"} groupoid cardinality
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi χ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi χ
                      %mi homotop
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\chi(C) = \chi_{homotop}(C)
                    \\,.
          %p
            This is noted in (
            %a{:href => "#Leinster"}> Leinster, example 2.7
            ).
          .num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              For instance for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+group"} finite group
              let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mi G
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B G \simeq K(G,1) \in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ho%28Top%29"} Ho(Top)
              be its
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization+of+categories"} geometric realization
              both of the one-object groupoids
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} *//G
              as well as of some finite
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mi G
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    B G \simeq |*//G| \simeq |C|
                    \\,.
            %p
              By prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PosteEulerCharGiveSpaceCharUnderRealization"}
              we have that the categorical Euler characteristic of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is the topological Euler characteristic of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B G
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ReproducingGroupoidCardinality"}
              we have that the categorical Euler characteristic of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} *//G
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+cardinality"} homotopy cardinality
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B G
          %p
            Typically for one and the same
            = succeed "-groupoid," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %p
            However, by applying some standard apparent “tricks” on non-convergent series, often these can be made sense of after all, and then do agree with the other notion. For more on this see (
            %a{:href => "#Baez05"}> Baez05
            ).
          %h3#basic_relations_for_euler_characteristics_of_topological_spaces Basic relations for Euler characteristics of topological spaces
          %p
          #PoincareHopfTheorem.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poincar%C3%A9%E2%80%93Hopf+theorem"}> Poincaré–Hopf theorem
                )
              %br/
              (…)
          %p
          #EulerCharacteristicOfSpheres.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              %strong (Euler characteristic of spheres)
              %br/
              The Euler characteristic of an even dimensional sphere is 2, that of an odd dimensional sphere vanishes:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi χ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mn 2
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mtd
                              %mi n
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mtext is even
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mn 0
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mtd
                              %mtext otherwise
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\chi(S^{n})
                    \\;=\;
                    \\left\{
                    \\array{
                    2 &amp;\vert&amp; n \, \text{is even}
                    \\\
                    0 &amp;\vert&amp; \text{otherwise}
                    }
                    \\right.
            %p
          (e.g.
          = succeed ")" do
            %a{:href => "#Libgober"} Libgober, p. 16
          %p
          #EulerCharacteristicOfCoveringSpaces.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              %strong (Euler characteristic of covering spaces)
              %br/
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi q
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \xrightarrow{q} Y
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covering+space"} covering space
              over a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+topological+space"} connected topological space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/degree+of+a+continuous+function"} degree
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi deg
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} deg(q) \in \mathbb{N}
              (and the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+homology"} ordinary homology
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              is finitely generated) then the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euler+characteristic"} Euler characteristic
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi deg
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} deg(q)
              times that of
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi χ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi ord
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi χ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\chi(X) \,=\, ord(G) \cdot \chi(Y)
                    \\,.
            %p
          (e.g. topospaces
          = succeed ")" do
            %a{:href => "https://topospaces.subwiki.org/wiki/Euler_characteristic_of_covering_space_is_product_of_degree_of_covering_and_Euler_characteristic_of_base"} here
          %p
          #EulerCharacteristicOfConnectedSums.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euler+characteristic"} Euler characteristic
                of
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+sums"} connected sums
              %br/
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              be
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+manifolds"} closed manifolds
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+manifold"} topological
              or
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentiable+manifold"} differentiable
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/even+number"} even
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euler+characteristic"} Euler characteristic
              of their
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+sum"} connected sum
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sum"} sum
              of their separate
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euler+characteristics"} Euler characteristics
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi χ
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ♯
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi χ
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mo +
                    %mi χ
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mo −
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\chi
                    \\big(
                    X \sharp Y
                    \\big)
                    \\;=\;
                    \\chi
                    \\big(X\big)
                    +
                    \\chi
                    \\big(Y\big)
                    \-2
            %p
          (e.g.
          = succeed ")" do
            %a{:href => "http://math.ucr.edu/~res/miscpapers/csums+echars.pdf"} here
          %h3#gaussbonnet_theorem Gauss-Bonnet theorem
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            an even-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"}> dimension
            al
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integration"} integration
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+object"} infinitesimal
            data: this is the statement of the higher dimensional
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gauss-Bonnet+theorem"} Gauss-Bonnet theorem
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/magnitude+of+an+enriched+category"} magnitude of an enriched category
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euler+class"} Euler class
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifold+Euler+characteristic"} orbifold Euler characteristic
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arithmetic+genus"} arithmetic genus
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C-field+tadpole+cancellation"} C-field tadpole cancellation
          %h2#references References
          %p
            On
            = succeed "\u2018s" do
              %span.newWikiWord
                Leonard Euler
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Leonard+Euler"} ?
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polyhedra"} polyhedra
          %ul
            %li#CBG08
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+H.+Conway"}> John H. Conway
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heidi+Burgiel"} Heidi Burgiel
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chaim+Goodman-Strauss"} Chaim Goodman-Strauss
              = succeed "," do
                %em Euler’s Map Theorem
              = succeed "," do
                %em The Symmetries of Things
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.routledge.com/The-Symmetries-of-Things/Conway-Burgiel-Goodman-Strauss/p/book/9781568812205"} ISBN:9781568812205
          %p General review:
          %ul
            %li#Libgober
              Jonathan Libgober:
              %em The Euler characteristic, Poincaré–Hopf theorem, and applications
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.uchicago.edu/~may/VIGRE/VIGRE2010/REUPapers/Libgober.pdf"}> pdf
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Libgober_EulerCharacteristic.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p Textbook account:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edwin+Spanier"}> Edwin Spanier
              , p. 156 onwards in:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Algebraic topology
          %p
            Proof that the Euler characteristic is (up to the overall multiplicative factor) the only additive homotopy invariant of a
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+CW+complexes"} finite CW complexes
          %ul
            %li
              V. A. Efremovich, Yuli B. Rudyak,
              = succeed "," do
                %em On the concept of the Euler characteristic
              = succeed ":5(191)" do
                %strong 31
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=458412"} MR458412
              %a{:href => "http://www.mathnet.ru/php/getFT.phtml?jrnid=rm&paperid=3975&volume=31&year=1976&issue=5&fpage=239&what=fullt"} Russian pdf
          %p
            The description of Euler characteristics are categorical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trace"} traces
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+categories"} symmetric monoidal categories
            is discussed in section 4 of
          %ul
            %li#DoldPuppe
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Albrecht+Dold"}> Albrecht Dold
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dieter+Puppe"} Dieter Puppe
              %em Duality, trace and transfer
              , Proceedings of the Steklov Institute of Mathematics, (1984), issue 4
          %p
            Behaviour of tracial Euler characteristic under
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+colimit"} homotopy colimits
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#May
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+May"}> Peter May
              ,
              %em The additivity of traces in triangulated categories
              K-theory (1991) (
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.uiuc.edu/K-theory/0474/"}> website
              )
          %p Textbooks on combinatorial aspects of Euler characteristic include
          %ul
            %li#Stanley
              %p
                Richard P. Stanley,
                %em Enumerative Combinatorics
                , Vol. I, Cambridge Studies in Advanced Mathematics 49, Cambridge University Press, corrected reprint (1997)
            %li#Rota
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gian-Carlo+Rota"}> Gian-Carlo Rota
                ,
                %em On the foundations of combinatorial theory I: theory of Möbius functions
                , Z. Wahrscheinlichkeitstheorie und Verw. Gebiete 2 (1964), 340–368.
          %p
            The Euler characteristic of a smooth manifold as its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+category"} stable homotopy category
            is discussed in example 3.7 of
          %ul
            %li#PontoShulman
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kate+Ponto"}> Kate Ponto
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Shulman"} Mike Shulman
              %em Traces in symmetric monoidal categories
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.sandiego.edu/~shulman/papers/traces_sym.pdf"}> pdf
              ,
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "http://www.sandiego.edu/~shulman/papers/ccrtraces.pdf"} slides
          %p
            See
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+spectrum"} Thom spectrum
            for more on this
          %p
            The Euler characteristic of groupoids –
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid+cardinality"} groupoid cardinality
            – has been amplified in
          %ul
            %li#BaezDolan
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Baez"}> John Baez
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+Dolan"} James Dolan
              %em From Finite Sets to Feynman Diagrams
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math.QA/0004133"}> arXiv
              )
          %p
            An exposition with an eye towards the relation between Euler characteristic and
            = succeed "-groupoid" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %ul#Baez05
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Baez"}> John Baez
              ,
              %em The mysteries of counting: Euler characteristic versus homotopy cardinality
              (
              %a{:href => "http://math.ucr.edu/home/baez/counting/"}> web
              ) Lecture notes (2005)
          %p
            A treatment of this relation using
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Morava+K-theories"} Morava K-theories
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              Lior Yanovski,
              %em Homotopy Cardinality via Extrapolation of Morava-Euler Characteristics
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2303.02603"}> arXiv:2303.02603
              )
          %p
            The role of homotopy cardinality in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization"} quantization
            is touched on towards the end of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Freed"}> Daniel Freed
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Hopkins"} Mike Hopkins
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"} Jacob Lurie
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Constantin+Teleman"} Constantin Teleman
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Topological+Quantum+Field+Theories+from+Compact+Lie+Groups"} Topological Quantum Field Theories from Compact Lie Groups
          %p The generalization of the definition of Euler characteristic from posets to categories is due to
          %ul
            %li
              %p#Leinster
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tom+Leinster"}> Tom Leinster
                ,
                %em The Euler characteristic of a category
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0610260"}> arXiv:0610260
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tom+Leinster"}> Tom Leinster
                ,
                %em The Euler characteristic of a category as a sum of a divergent series
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0707.0835"}> arXiv:0707.0835
                )
          %p
            The compatibility of Euler characteristic of categories with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+colimits"} homotopy colimits
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+M.+Fiore"}> Thomas M. Fiore
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wolfgang+L%C3%BCck"} Wolfgang Lück
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Roman+Sauer"} Roman Sauer
              %em Euler Characteristics of Categories and Homotopy Colimits
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1007.3868"}> arXiv:1007.3868
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p More on Euler characteristics of categories is in
          %ul
            %li
              Kazunori Noguchi,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The Euler characteristic of infinite acyclic categories with filtrations
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1004.2547"} arxiv/1004.2547
          %p On “Negative sets” and Euler characteristic:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9+Joyal"}> André Joyal
                ,
                %em Regle des signes en algebre combinatoire
                , Comptes Rendus Mathematiques de l’Academie des Sciences, La Societe Royale du Canada VII (1985), 285-290.
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Steve+Schanuel"}> Steve Schanuel
                ,
                %em Negative sets have Euler characteristic and dimension
                , Lecture Notes in Mathematics 1488, Springer Verlag, Berlin, 1991, pp. 379-385.
            %li
              %p
                Daniel Loeb,
                %em Sets with a negative number of elements
                , Adv. Math. 91 (1992), 64-74.
          %p Resumming divergent Euler characteristics:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                William J. Floyd, Steven P. Plotnick,
                %em Growth functions on Fuchsian groups and the Euler characteristic
                , Invent. Math. 88 (1987), 1-29.
            %li
              %p
                R. I. Grigorchuk,
                %em Growth functions, rewriting systems and Euler characteristic
                , Mat. Zametki 58 (1995), 653-668, 798.
            %li
              %p
                James Propp,
                %em Exponentiation and Euler measure
                , Algebra Universalis 49 (2003), 459-471. (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0204009"}> arXiv:math.CO/0204009
                ).
            %li
              %p
                James Propp,
                %em Euler measure as generalized cardinality
                \. (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0203289"}> arXiv
                ).
          %p Euler characteristics of tame spaces:
          %ul
            %li
              Lou van den Dries,
              %em Tame Topology and O-Minimal Structures
              Cambridge U. Press, Cambridge, 1998. Chapter 4.2: Euler Characteristic.
          %p Euler characteristics of groups:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                G. Harder,
                %em A Gauss-Bonnet formula for discrete arithmetically defined groups
                , Ann. Sci. Ecole Norm. Sup. 4 (1971), 409-455.
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Pierre+Serre"}> Jean-Pierre Serre
                ,
                %em Cohomologie des groups discretes
                , Ann. Math. Studies 70 (1971), 77-169.
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kenneth+Brown"}> Kenneth Brown
                ,
                %em Euler characteristics, in Cohomology of Groups
                , Graduate Texts in Mathematics 182, Springer, 1982, pp. 230-272.
            %li
              %p
                O. Y. Viro,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Some integral calculus based on Euler characteristic
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 1346
                %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1007/BFb0082775"} doi
          %p Complex cardinalities:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Andreas Blass,
                %em Seven trees in one
                , Jour. Pure Appl. Alg. 103 (1995), 1-21. (
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.lsa.umich.edu/~ablass/cat.html"}> web
                )
            %li
              %p
                Robbie Gates,
                %em
                  On the generic solution to
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi P
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P(X) = X
                  in distributive categories
                , Jour. Pure Appl. Alg. 125 (1998), 191-212.
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marcelo+Fiore"}> Marcelo Fiore
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tom+Leinster"} Tom Leinster
                %em An objective representation of the Gaussian integers
                , Jour. Symb. Comp. 37 (2004), 707-716. (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0211454"}> arXiv
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marcelo+Fiore"}> Marcelo Fiore
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tom+Leinster"} Tom Leinster
                %em Objects of categories as complex numbers
                , Adv. Math. 190 (2005), 264-277 (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0212377"}> arXiv:0212377
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marcelo+Fiore"}> Marcelo Fiore
                ,
                %em Isomorphisms of generic recursive polynomial types
                , to appear in 31st Symposium on Principles of Programming Languages (POPL04). (
                %a{:href => "http://www.cl.cam.ac.uk/~mpf23/papers/Types/recisos.ps.gz"}> ps
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C.+T.+C.+Wall"}> C. T. C. Wall
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Arithmetic invariants of subdivision of complexes
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.4153/CJM-1966-012-9"} doi
                %a{:href => "http://cms.math.ca/cjm/v18/cjm1966v18.0092-0096.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi A
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{A}^1
            \-Euler characteristic
          %ul
            %li
              Arcila-Maya, Niny; Bethea, Candace; Opie, Morgan; Wickelgren, Kirsten; Zakharevich, Inna,
